On Saturday 05 February 2011 22:23:44 .alyn.post. wrote:
> On Sat, Feb 05, 2011 at 06:32:55PM +0100, Timo Paulssen wrote:
>> > I personally like the sound of {bu'umemi}
> >
> > mu'o mi'e timos
>
> That is very nice!  I like it.  It doesn't have the same imperative
> component that {ko} does, does it?  It's this saying "something is
> coincindent with me"?

"bu'u me mi" means "here I am". It's not an imperative. "me" turns "mi" into a 
selbri, meaning "to be me". Similarly "bu'u me do", "va me do", etc.

